Dr. S. Murali is a highly skilled doctor with a strong background in stroke care. His memberships in professional organisations, multilingual proficiency, and various honours and assignments attest to his commitment to patient care, medical practice advancement, and education. Dr. Murali is a well-respected figure and a great asset to the medical industry - thanks to his contributions to and leadership in the field of neurology. He is a faculty member for the postgraduate teaching programme at the National Board of Examination and mentors postgraduate students in neurology. He also serves as the Manipal Hospitals&#39; Regional Chief of Clinical Service and teaches neurology at the Manipal Academy of Higher Education on a part-time basis. Dr. Murali also serves as a principal assessor and educator for the NABH, which is an organisation that accredits hospitals and other healthcare organisations. In addition, he serves as a senator for the Rajiv Gandhi University of Health Sciences and is the chief host examiner for the UK&#39;s MRCP (Membership of the Royal College of Physicians).&quot;

Dr. Davinder Singh Chadha is a well-known Interventional Cardiology Consultant who is currently associated with Manipal Hospital, Old Airport Road, Bangalore. Dr. Chadha also holds considerable experience in intravascular lithotripsy, the treatment of arrhythmias with ablation and pacemakers, coronary artery surgery, the treatment of congestive heart failure, intravascular imaging, implantation, CRT devices, coronary interventions, structural heart disease, cardiac outpatient procedures, endovascular interventions, left main angioplasty, TAVI, rotational atherectomy, and bifurcation angioplasty. He graduated with MBBS from AFMC Pune University and acquired his M.D. in Medicine from AFMC Pune University in Pune, Maharashtra. He also pursued his D.M. in Cardiology from the same university. Dr. Chadha further pursued Hons in FRCP (E). He went on to acquire his fellowship from the Royal College of Physicians in the U.K. He has been the Examiner in D.M. (Cardiology) at RGUH Bangalore, Pune University, and Tamil Nadu University in Vellore. Dr. Chadha is an acclaimed interventional cardiologist at Old Airport Road.&nbsp;

Dr. Davinder Singh Chadha has worked in the medical field for over 23 years in the field of cardiology. Over the years of his service, he performed numerous OCT procedures. He has performed more than over 400 rotational atherectomy surgeries and nearly 10000 non-coronary and coronary intervention surgeries over the past years. Moreover, he operated several complicated interventions comprising carotid and BTK. In South India, he also conducted intravascular lithotripsy operations for calcific coronary artery disease. Dr. Chadha created the TAVI program at each Command health centre in Bangalore and AFMC Pune, where he has performed 12 TAVI surgeries in the last two years. He conducted the first TAVI operation in 2016. He is praised for his kind and compassionate treatment of his patients. He is also fluent in speaking languages like English, Hindi, and Punjabi.

Dr. Chadha&rsquo;s talks and publications include papers in national as well as international journals. For his work on Trans collateral Renal Angioplasty for a completely Occluded Renal Artery, he was awarded the Best Challenging Case Award. Notably, He received the important HQ Southern Command Gold Medal, the Silver Medal, and the General B. Basu Rolling Trophy for finishing first in college in Ophthalmology in the final MBBS test. He also received a Gold Medal for achieving first place in college in surgical procedures in the most recent MBBS exams. Some of the services provided by the doctor include FFR (fractional flow reserve), trans-oesophageal ECHO, Dobutamine stress test, device closure for congenital heart diseases, ambulatory blood pressure monitoring, PAMI, Holter monitoring, TAVI (transcatheter aortic valve implantation), pacemaker implantation, acute aortic dissection, repair of adult coarctation, and Patent Ductus Arteriosus device closure. Dr. Davinder Singh Chadha has also served as the main investigator on several international and ICMR-funded clinical trials, and he has published over 70 publications in national and international journals.

Dr. Vishwanath S is the best nephrologist in Bangalore, Old Airport Road, currently practising at Manipal Hospital Old Airport Road as a HOD &amp; Consultant - Nephrology and Transplant Physician. He holds more than 29 years of experience and has worked for 17 years as a specialist in Nephrology and is proficient in managing kidney problems in both adults and children, establishing him as the best nephrologist and transplant physician in Bangalore. He is the foremost&nbsp;Consultant Nephrology Oldairportroad, Bangalore

With a special interest in Clinical Nephrology, Dr. Vishwanath&#39;s extensive expertise in kidney care includes a large subset of renal diseases like Acute and Chronic Kidney Disease, Acute Renal Failure, Polycystic Kidney Disease, and more. He has vast experience in areas related to renal procedures, such as Renal Transplant, Swap Transplant, Paired Exchange Transplant, Dual Transplants (Kidney-Pancreas and Kidney-Liver), Hemodialysis, Peritoneal Dialysis (CAPD - Continuous ambulatory peritoneal dialysis and CCPD - Continuous cyclic peritoneal dialysis), Critical Care, Central Line Placement, and Catheter Placement.&nbsp;

From the academic front, Dr. Vishwanath S entered the field of medicine with an MBBS degree in 1995, followed by a DNB - Paediatrics and a DNB - Nephrology. He was awarded the prestigious Dr. HL Trivedi Gold Medal in DNB - Nephrology from the National Board of Examinations for securing the 1st rank at the all-India DNB Nephrology Examination. Dr. Vishwanath also has a Dr. PS Aniker, D.CH Gold Medal of Mysore University to his name for his MBBS Degree examination. He holds memberships at various organizations such as Member of National Academy of Medical Sciences (MNAMS), a Life Member of the Indian Academy of Paediatrics, Member of Indian Society of Nephrology, and Member of Indian Society of Transplantation.

Besides his clinical duties, Dr. Vishwanath is very active in medical literature and has authored multiple publications and distributions of journals at the national and international levels. His literature addressed topics such as &quot;Post Cov-19 kidney complications&quot;, &quot;The psychological aspect of organ donation in the current scenario&quot;, &quot;Busting myths and misconceptions over organ donation: A doctor speaks&quot;, and more. With his role as the HOD of the Nephrology Department at Manipal Hospital Old Airport Road, Dr. Vishwanath aims to offer patients with renal problems the best of medical care that is at par with international standards.&quot;

